The '''Museum''' is a a [[Location]] found within the {{Zone|Village}} on the [[Hub Island]]. It serves as a place for players to donate items in exchange for turning them [[Soulbound|Co-op Soulbound]] and {{SkyBlock XP}}.

== Purpose ==
The '''Museum''' allows players to donate items to {{NPCSprite|Madame Eleanor Q. Goldsworth III}}. When an accepted item is donated for the first time, the player is rewarded with permanent {{SkyBlock XP}}, and the item becomes [[Soulbound|Co-op Soulbound]], meaning it cannot be traded with anyone outside of the player's [[Co-op]] (if they have one).

More valuable items reward more {{SkyBlock XP}}. The Museum is split into categories based on [[Skills]], including {{Skill|Combat}}, {{Skill|Farming}}, {{Skill|Mining}}, {{Skill|Fishing}}, {{Skill|Foraging}}, {{Skill|Dungeoneering}}, and {{Skill|Hunting}}. There is also a Special Items category, in which items donated do not reward any {{SkyBlock XP}}, nor become become [[Soulbound|Co-op Soulbound]]. This category has a limit of 48 items.

[[Armor]] and [[Equipment]] sets can only be donated as a complete set, meaning individual pieces cannot be donated alone. When an item is donated, its creation date, date of donation, and position number (when below 50,000) can be seen. If an item is one of the first 1,000 created, then its number can be seen above the item when displayed in the Museum in one of the display cases.

Players on [[Stranded]] and [[Bingo]] profiles cannot access the Museum.

